      "rationale": "No test pins those sentences, so the two edits stand as they are. Nothing else is needed.\n\nI changed two harness pages and nothing else. In `plugins/core/skills/crew/references/audit.md`, the signature section now tells the lead, when presenting the report, to name what the verdict rests on the way the findings do: the failing test by its file or the test run's log, the lint error by its file and line, and a secret by the file the secrets run named or its log, never by quoting it, since the report's text passed through the scanner and the lead's message does not. It also says the message must state plainly that the report is unsigned and waits for the user to sign, and that an unsigned audit is neither proven nor done. In `plugins/core/skills/crew/references/deliver.md`, the audit paragraph gained the same rule in one clause: each defect named by path and line or log, a secret never by its value. The failing grader judges the final message alone, on exactly those terms: the key named by path or log and never by value, the failing test and lint error named, the report unsigned. The delivery text previously asked only for the verdict, counts, omissions and the PDF's absence, so whether the lead named locations or kept the key's value out depended on the model's own habit, which is what the split votes show. The brief-per-todo grader was already passing and I did not touch anything it reads.",
